---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getMediaAsset } from '../data/media-manifest';

const title = 'About USIVA | A US Council Planning Companion';
const description = 'How USIVA helps people and organizations with visa and immigration planning across temporary and permanent pathways, official sources, and responsible handoffs.';
const canonical = 'https://usiva.org/about.html';
const recordsPhoto = getMediaAsset('family-records');
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  activePath="/about.html"
  canonical={canonical}
  topbarMessage="Informational planning · verify current instructions with the responsible authority."
  topbarLink={{ label: 'Open official tools', href: '/official-tools.html' }}
>
  <section class="about-intro" aria-labelledby="page-title">
    <div class="shell-container about-intro__grid">
      <div class="about-intro__copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">About / the short version</p>
        <h1 id="page-title">USIVA is a planning companion for organizing the next decision.</h1>
        <p class="about-intro__lede">USIVA is the US Council’s public visa and immigration planning companion. It gives individuals, families, employers, and organizations a clear place to organize records, timing, authorization questions, and official-source checks across the categories that may fit their purpose.</p>
        <nav class="intro-actions" aria-label="About next steps">
          <a class="button button--primary" href="/services.html">See planning lanes</a>
          <a class="button button--outline" href="/visa-categories.html">Browse visa categories</a>
        </nav>
      </div>

      <figure class="about-figure">
        <img
          src={recordsPhoto.src}
          width={recordsPhoto.width}
          height={recordsPhoto.height}
          alt={recordsPhoto.alt}
          sizes="(min-width: 900px) 38vw, 100vw"
          loading="eager"
          fetchpriority="high"
        />
        <figcaption>{recordsPhoto.caption}</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section about-role" aria-labelledby="role-heading">
    <div class="shell-container about-role__grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">A practical role</p>
        <h2 id="role-heading">Make the question easier to verify.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="about-copy flow">
        <p>International planning often holds several timelines at once: academic preparation, funding, travel, school instructions, research opportunities, and the authorization boundaries that apply to each stage. USIVA gives those questions a visible place before deadline pressure makes them harder to separate.</p>
        <p>The site is intentionally source-aware. It helps a reader name a missing document, prepare a question for a designated school official or sponsor, and recognize when personal facts require licensed immigration counsel. The authority responsible for the case owns eligibility and other live decisions.</p>
        <aside class="relationship-note" aria-labelledby="relationship-heading">
          <h3 id="relationship-heading">Where USIVA sits</h3>
          <p>USIVA is a US Council companion. It works alongside a university, employer, sponsor, or connected research-program conversation while each provider remains responsible for its own instructions and outcomes.</p>
          <a href="https://usfellows.org/international-rd-scholars.html" rel="noreferrer">See the connected research-program reference at US Fellows <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--mist" aria-labelledby="principles-heading">
    <div class="shell-container principles-grid">
      <header>
        <p class="eyebrow">The editorial standard</p>
        <h2 id="principles-heading">Four habits keep a planning page honest.</h2>
        <p>These are working principles for public information; each person’s case receives its own review by the responsible authority.</p>
      </header>

      <ol class="principles-list">
        <li><span>01</span><div><h3>Start with the decision</h3><p>Ask what must be decided, by whom, and by when before collecting an indiscriminate stack of documents.</p></div></li>
        <li><span>02</span><div><h3>Make the boundary explicit</h3><p>Study, training, research exposure, assistantship, travel, and employment can have different rules. Name the activity before assuming it is allowed.</p></div></li>
        <li><span>03</span><div><h3>Leave a source trail</h3><p>Public rules, school instructions, sponsor guidance, and professional advice should be checked at the point of use and dated.</p></div></li>
        <li><span>04</span><div><h3>Know when to hand off</h3><p>Personal history, a prior refusal, a status concern, or a complicated work question deserves individualized advice from the right authority.</p></div></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section about-boundary" aria-labelledby="boundary-heading">
    <div class="shell-container about-boundary__grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--light">Plain language</p>
        <h2 id="boundary-heading">USIVA’s role in the planning system.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="boundary-columns">
        <div>
          <h3>USIVA is</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>A public planning companion for study, research, family, and employer questions.</li>
            <li>A place to organize records, timing, source checks, and handoffs.</li>
            <li>A bridge to official tools and the authority that controls the next answer.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Where the decision lives</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Legal advice and representation come from qualified immigration counsel.</li>
            <li>Current instructions come from the university, sponsor, consular post, government agency, or employer.</li>
            <li>Admission, employment, funding, visa issuance, and government approval come from the responsible authority.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section about-references" aria-labelledby="references-heading">
    <div class="shell-container">
      <header class="references-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Continue with a purpose</p>
        <h2 id="references-heading">Choose the reference that answers your next question.</h2>
      </header>
      <ul class="reference-list">
        <li><a href="/visa.html"><strong>Visa directory</strong><span>Start with a route overview and follow its official-source handoff.</span></a></li>
        <li><a href="/visa-categories.html"><strong>Visa categories</strong><span>Compare temporary, study, work, family, and permanent-route groupings.</span></a></li>
        <li><a href="/employers.html"><strong>Employer resources</strong><span>Orient I-9, E-Verify, and employer-side questions before a handoff.</span></a></li>
        <li><a href="/official-tools.html"><strong>Official tools</strong><span>Use government case-status, visa, and employer resources directly.</span></a></li>
        <li><a href="/briefs.html"><strong>Research briefs</strong><span>Read short, source-led notes about planning and compliance questions.</span></a></li>
        <li><a href="/articles.html"><strong>Articles</strong><span>Follow longer explanations as general planning content.</span></a></li>
      </ul>
      <p class="source-note">For current instructions, begin with <a href="https://www.uscis.gov/" rel="noreferrer">USCIS</a>, the <a href="https://travel.state.gov/content/travel/en/us-visas.html" rel="noreferrer">U.S. Department of State</a>, or the school, sponsor, and employer responsible for the matter.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-intro {
    background: var(--color-mist);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line);
  }

  .about-intro__grid {
    align-items: end;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(18rem, 0.78fr);
    padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4.5rem);
  }

  .about-intro__copy {
    max-width: 58rem;
  }

  .about-intro h1 {
    max-width: 18ch;
  }

  .about-intro__lede {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    margin-block-start: var(--space-2);
    max-width: 58ch;
  }

  .intro-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-1);
    margin-block-start: var(--space-3);
  }

  .about-figure {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .about-figure img {
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 3;
    object-fit: cover;
    width: 100%;
  }

  figcaption {
    border-inline-start: 2px solid var(--color-gold);
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    line-height: 1.45;
    margin-block-start: var(--space-1);
    padding-inline-start: var(--space-1);
  }

  .about-role__grid,
  .principles-grid,
  .about-boundary__grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.75fr) minmax(0, 1.25fr);
  }

  .about-role h2,
  .principles-grid h2,
  .about-boundary h2,
  .references-heading h2 {
    max-width: 22ch;
  }

  .about-copy {
    max-width: 62ch;
  }

  .relationship-note {
    border-block: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    margin-block-start: var(--space-3);
    padding-block: var(--space-2);
  }

  .relationship-note h3 {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
  }

  .relationship-note a,
  .source-note a {
    color: var(--color-accent-dark);
    font-weight: 750;
  }

  .principles-grid > header {
    max-width: 30rem;
  }

  .principles-list {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line-dark);
    list-style: none;
  }

  .principles-list li {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    grid-template-columns: 2.3rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    padding-block: var(--space-2);
  }

  .principles-list li > span {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }

  .principles-list h3 {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    margin-block-end: 0.25rem;
  }

  .principles-list p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .about-boundary {
    background: var(--color-navy);
    color: var(--color-paper);
  }

  .about-boundary h2,
  .about-boundary h3 {
    color: var(--color-paper);
  }

  .boundary-columns {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
  }

  .boundary-columns > div {
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.35);
    padding-block-start: var(--space-2);
  }

  .boundary-columns h3 {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
  }

  .boundary-columns ul {
    color: var(--color-on-dark-muted);
    padding-inline-start: 1.15rem;
  }

  .boundary-columns li + li {
    margin-block-start: 0.65rem;
  }

  .about-references {
    background: var(--color-paper);
  }

  .references-heading {
    max-width: 48rem;
  }

  .reference-list {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    list-style: none;
    margin-block-start: var(--space-3);
  }

  .reference-list li {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line);
  }

  .reference-list a {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.3rem 1.5rem;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(11rem, 0.5fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    padding-block: var(--space-2);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .reference-list strong {
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .reference-list span {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }

  .source-note {
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    margin-block-start: var(--space-3);
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .about-intro__grid,
    .about-role__grid,
    .principles-grid,
    .about-boundary__grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .about-figure {
      max-width: 42rem;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .intro-actions .button {
      width: 100%;
    }

    .boundary-columns,
    .reference-list a {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
